+/// Whether this record's colour 0 is a multisample source with no prior
+/// contents this rail could offer it: a resolving attachment at the start of
+/// its guest encoder.
+///
+/// Every door a LOAD walks -- the provenance seed, the APV pair, the mapper
+/// seed, the GVA elision and the resident chain -- names the *resolve target*:
+/// a resolving colour's `texture_ref`, `mapping_id` and `target_seed` describe
+/// the single-sample destination, never the multisample source, which has no
+/// CPU-visible storage at all. Metal discards that source once its resolve-only
+/// store runs, so an encoder that starts by loading it reads undefined contents
+/// on the device too. The lawful translation begins the attachment undefined
+/// (`Color0Load::Undefined`, elected by the engine from the declared action)
+/// and spends nothing on a seed that could only reach the wrong image. A
+/// continued record is the other case: the engine keeps the source open for the
+/// whole encoder and its LOAD is what the records before it rendered.
+fn multisample_source_begins_undefined(req: &DrawEncodeRequest) -> bool {
+    !req.continues_render_pass
+        && req
+            .colors
+            .first()
+            .is_some_and(|color| color.multisample_source_ref != 0)
+}
